    "q-556448": {
      "dom_id": "step-q556448",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Between which two consecutive tenths does $\\sqrt[3]{80}$ lie?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the two consecutive tenths between which $\\sqrt[3]{80}$ lies, we need to find two numbers with one decimal place whose cubes bracket $80$.\n\nFirst, let's establish between which two consecutive integers $\\sqrt[3]{80}$ lies.\nWe know that ${4}^{3}=64$ and ${5}^{3}=125$.\nSince $64<80<125$, we know that $4<\\sqrt[3]{80}<5$.\n\nNext, we can test decimals between $4$ and $5$ to narrow down the interval:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{4.2}^{3} & =74.088 \\\\ {4.3}^{3} & =79.507 \\\\ {4.4}^{3} & =85.184\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $79.507<80<85.184$, we can write:\n\n$$\n{4.3}^{3}<80<{4.4}^{3}\n$$\n\nTaking the cube root of each part of the inequality gives:\n\n$$\n4.3<\\sqrt[3]{80}<4.4\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\sqrt[3]{80}$ lies between $4.3$ and $4.4$.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
