    "q-556460": {
      "dom_id": "step-q556460",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Between which two consecutive whole numbers does $\\sqrt{55}$ lie?",
      "worked_solution": "To find which two consecutive whole numbers $\\sqrt{55}$ lies between, we first identify the perfect squares that are just below and just above $55.$\n\nThe perfect squares closest to $55$ are $49$ and $64.$ We have\n\n$$\n49<55<64.\n$$\n\nTaking the square root of each number, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{49} & <\\sqrt{55}<\\sqrt{64} \\\\ 7 & <\\sqrt{55}<8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14239128/assets/71bc6c197bd0fb3444a7105d8da77ead56cde1da0bb76139668778bfb4b3cd22.png)\n\nTherefore, $\\sqrt{55}$ lies between $7$ and $8.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
